 "help": "usage: wgsextract sign create [-h] [--output OUTPUT] [--key KEY] PATH [PATH ...]\n\npositional arguments:\n  PATH             Files or directories to sign.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help       show this help message and exit\n  --output OUTPUT  Manifest path. Defaults to <outdir>/SHA256SUMS, or SHA256SUMS in the inputs'\n                   common directory.\n  --key KEY        OpenSSH private key (or public key held by ssh-agent) to sign with. Defaults to\n                   the signing_key setting; without either, only the checksum manifest is written.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract sign create results/\n  wgsextract sign create results/ --key ~/.ssh/id_ed25519\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  SHA256SUMS in the inputs' folder (or --output); SHA256SUMS.sig with --key.\n\nneeds:\n  no external tools; depending on options and inputs, also: ssh-keygen;\n  minutes for genome-sized files.\n",
